#: ../pwntools/docs/source/windbg.rst:6
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib.windbg` --- Working with WinDbg"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:1
msgid ""
"During exploit development, it is frequently useful to debug the target "
"binary under WinDbg. This module provides a simple interface to do so "
"under Windows."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:5
msgid ""
"By default, :attr:`.context.debugger` is set to ``\"auto\"``, which will "
"attempt to automatically select an appropriate debugger based on the "
"available debuggers on the system."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:9
msgid "The order of preference is: - ``windbgx`` - ``windbg`` - ``x64dbg``"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:14
msgid ""
"If automatic lookup fails, you can manually set :attr:`.context.debugger`"
" to the debugger of your choice and provide the path to the debugger "
"binary using :attr:`.context.windbgx_binary`, "
":attr:`.context.windbg_binary`, or :attr:`.context.x64dbg_binary`."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:20
msgid "Useful Functions"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:22
msgid ":func:`attach` - Attach to an existing process"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:23
msgid ":func:`debug` - Start a new process under the debugger"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:26
msgid "Debugging Tips"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:28
msgid ""
"The :func:`attach` and :func:`debug` functions will likely be your bread "
"and butter for debugging."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:31
msgid ""
"Both allow you to provide a script to pass to WinDbg when it is started, "
"so that it can automatically set your breakpoints."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:35
msgid "Attaching to Processes"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:37
msgid ""
"To attach to an existing process, just use :func:`attach`.  You can pass "
"a PID, a process name (including file extension), or a :class:`.process`."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:41
msgid "Spawning New Processes"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:43
msgid ""
"Attaching to processes with :func:`attach` is useful, but the state the "
"process is in may vary.  If you need to attach to a process very early, "
"and debug it from the very first instruction (or even the start of "
"``main``), you instead should use :func:`debug`."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:48
msgid ""
"When you use :func:`debug`, the return value is a :class:`.tube` object "
"that you interact with exactly like normal."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:52
msgid "Tips and Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:55
msgid "``NOPTRACE`` magic argument"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:57
msgid "It's quite cumbersom to comment and un-comment lines containing `attach`."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.windbg:59
msgid ""
"You can cause these lines to be a no-op by running your script with the "
"``NOPTRACE`` argument appended, or with ``PWNLIB_NOPTRACE=1`` in the "
"environment. (The name is borrowed from ptrace syscall on Linux.)"
msgstr ""

